 mirroring sibling packages (typescript/vite/vitest/wrangler from catalog:, @types/node). Add a DEPENDENCY on the upstream toolkit via relative source import (do NOT add it to pnpm dependencies — import via a relative path like ../../cloudflare-os/packages/integration-tests/src/harness.ts, since it is source-only and not published; check how the kernel's own workshop-evals package imports it and mirror that exactly — read cloudflare-os/packages/workshop-evals/package.json and its imports).\n2. tsconfig.json — mirror the sibling packages' tsconfig (extends ../../cloudflare-os/tsconfig.json, paths for @gadgets/stage etc., include src).\n3. vite.config.ts + vitest.config.ts — mirror siblings (vitest include __tests__/*.test.ts).\n4. src/harness-adapter.ts — the adapter: a function that maps our OUTER gatekeeper package dirs + the kernel's workshop-backend dir into whatever startHarness/createHarness accepts (WorkerConfig[]), with an explicit \"WORKS ONLY IF upstream resolves arbitrary absolute dirs\" verification: if harness.ts hardcodes paths relative to its own location such that external dirs cannot work, write a clearly-commented adapter that copies each needed wrangler.jsonc into an in-memory WorkerConfig instead (name/main/build/services/vars from the package's own wrangler.jsonc parsed with jsonc-parser). Document every assumption in comments. Do NOT import cloudflare:workers anywhere.\n5. __tests__/smoke.test.ts — ONE test that asserts the adapter builds WorkerConfigs for workshop-backend + gatekeeper-snowflake + gatekeeper-nvidia from their real wrangler.jsonc files (pure file/parse assertions, NO wrangler boot, NO network). This must pass under plain `npx vitest run` in node.\n6. src/scenarios.ts — empty exported stubs documenting scenarios A-E (names + one-line intent each, from the plan). No implementations.\n\nConstraints: NO implementation of scenario logic beyond stubs. NO changes outside packages/operating-environment-tests/. Plain JSON5 comments not needed — keep configs minimal and valid.\n\nWhen done, run `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npx vitest run` inside the new package and iterate until both pass (vitest may fail if workspace deps are unlinked — if so, say so explicitly in your final line; do NOT run pnpm install).\nOUTPUT: the new package directory only. When done print: DONE packages/operating-environment-tests tsc=<pass|fail> vitest=<pass|fail|blocked>"}],"timestamp":1789538972616}}
